# SYNTHETIC fixture. Not a captured sweep, and it cannot be one: a
# sw:notMeasuredReason of "prober-failed" is published only when the task
# probing an endpoint's host panicked or was cancelled, so producing it live
# would mean shipping a prober that crashes.
#
# The quads below were not hand-written either. They are the output of
# prober/src/emit.rs's emit_nquads, called with hand-built inputs: the eight
# metrics of prober/metrics.toml against one endpoint, seven of them (every
# "cheap" one) as NotMeasuredReason::ProberFailed and metric:classes (the one
# "expensive" one) as NotMeasuredReason::CostCeiling, with max_cost "cheap",
# concurrency 2 and failed_endpoints 1. That is exactly the shape
# prober/src/lib.rs's `assemble` produces for an endpoint whose group failed:
# every metric that would have run as prober-failed, every metric the cost
# ceiling had already declined as cost-ceiling, and NO
# sw:declarationsRead, because nothing was ever fetched.
#
# Regenerated on 2026-08-24 for stage 1c-b4, which splits emission into a
# header, one chunk per endpoint and a footer. It grew three quads: the
# header's sw:emission terminator, the chunk's sw:completedEndpoint
# terminator, and the footer's sw:finalised terminator, with
# sw:failedEndpoints moving from the header to the footer beside the last of
# them. This is the only committed fixture that claims to be current emitter
# output, so it is the only one that has to move when the emitter does; the
# captured historical sweeps (run-declined.nq and the rest) carry no
# terminator on purpose, and "neither terminator" is exactly the third case
# the scheme defines, a run from before it existed.
#
# Both reasons in one run is the point. The two are opposite claims about who
# is responsible, so a page that renders one sentence for every decline says
# something untrue about seven of these eight rows, and a fixture carrying
# only one reason cannot see that.
#
# 51 quads, one run graph (urn:sparqlwatch:run:2026-08-23T02:00:00Z), one
# endpoint (data.kkg.kadaster.nl/query, so that this run can be loaded beside
# the real 16:00 sweep of the same endpoint), 8 sw:NotMeasured facts, no
# dqv:QualityMeasurement, no sw:ContentSample. The subjects are the derived
# scheme of stage 1c-b3, because this run's emitter is the one that produces
# it.
